// Filling the fingerprint table, and recording which function each entry
// belongs to.
//
// `cfp` holds the fingerprints and `cfpfn` holds, for each one, the `prog`
// index of the function it came from. That is simply 0, 1, 2, ... -- one entry
// per function, a chained function included: a chain function is one unit of
// logic, fingerprinted whole (../canon/func/more/segs/chain.id). The two lists
// could be collapsed into one. They are kept apart so that the index of a
// fingerprint and the index of a function stay different things with
// different names, rather than one number used for both -- which is what
// `fname_at` (./more/report/dup.id) resolves, and the only place in the
// checker that maps one to the other.

uq_fill_all() {
  int i = 0;
  while(i < len((import prog))) {
    uq_fill_at(i);
    i = i + 1;
  }
} return void;
